  "limitations_and_imbalance_summary": [
    "Class Balance & Deduplication Shift: Exact-byte SHA-256 deduplication (0 duplicates removed) and perceptual dHash cluster grouping yield a post-cleaning max/min class ratio of 1.00x, mitigated via balanced inverse-frequency training class weights.",
    "Surface-Only Modality: RGB optical imaging captures external peel discoloration, fungal lesions, and shriveling, but cannot detect internal core rot, early enzymatic browning beneath thick rinds (e.g., pomegranate or orange), or invisible microbial/chemical hazards.",
    "Closed-Set Domain Assumption: Softmax probabilities sum to 1.0 across the 8 trained fruit species. Uploading unsupported produce (e.g., mango, avocado) can trigger uncertain predictions, flagged in production when top-1 confidence falls below 60%.",
    "Lowest Held-Out F1 Subclasses: Fresh Pomegranate (F1=0.923), Rotten Banana (F1=0.923), Rotten Guava (F1=0.923), where dark natural skin pigmentation or specular highlights resemble early bruising."
  ],
